00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:49.680
to them, right. Oftentimes when we speak even as I'm&nbsp;
recording this video right now and speaking like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:55.680
I can't hear myself talking and really process&nbsp;
that and think about what I'm going to say next.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.680 --> 00:08:01.360
So, when you reflect what somebody else says,&nbsp;
it illuminates what they're saying to them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:05.280
And oftentimes it's amazing like even if you&nbsp;
reflect verbatim, exactly what somebody else has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:09.760
said, you reflect that back to them, it's amazing&nbsp;
how frequently someone will jump and be like, "No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:14.480
no. That's not what I mean." And then correct and&nbsp;
extend that conversation and get to the heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:19.680
of the matter. It's a phenomenal tool to create&nbsp;
conversations that matter to you and to the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:26.880
person. Now, a reflective question is you reflect a&nbsp;
piece of what somebody said and then add on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:30.960
a question. Let's do this kind of odd in a video&nbsp;
format right now. So, we're having an interaction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.600
right you're watching a video which I've recorded&nbsp;
